BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free 30-Minute Dance Shows on Freedom + Justice at SF Libraries (O
 ct. 3-17)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T151500
DTSTAMP:20260927T032919Z
UID:funcheap-20261003-free30minutedanceshowson
CATEGORIES:community,free
DESCRIPTION:https://sf.funcheap.com/free-30minute-dance-shows-freedom-just
 ice-sf-libraries-oct-317/\nLocation: san francisco\nPrice: Free\nCategorie
 s: community\, free\nSource: funcheap/san-francisco\n\nOctober 3 – 17: S
 hows at 1pm and 3:15pm each Saturday Flyaway Productions returns to the st
 reets with a new dance-based public art project exploring the concept of f
 reedom at the intersection of public libraries and prisons. Directed by Fl
 yaway Artistic Director Jo Kreiter in coalition with the San Francisco Pub
 lic Library\, ‘Freedom Comes’ features a cast of seven female dancers\
 , original research and text by April Harris\, and commissioned music by K
 alyn Harwood. A total of six 30-minute shows are scheduled at 1 p.m. and 3
 :15 p.m. over three consecutive Saturdays\, October 3 – 17. ‘Freedom C
 omes’ opens October 3 at Visitacion Valley Branch Library before moving 
 to the San Francisco Main Library on October 10\, and finally to the Orteg
 a Branch Library on October 17. All shows are free with no reservation req
 uired. Flyaway’s primary collaborator is April Harris\, an incarcerated 
 writer serving a life sentence at the California Institution for Women in 
 Corona\, California. She is currently a research advocate to support the U
 niversity of California Sentencing Project\, a collaboration between the U
 niversity of California at San Diego and Los Angeles\, and members of the 
 California Coalition
LOCATION:san francisco
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/free-30minute-dance-shows-freedom-justice-sf-l
 ibraries-oct-317/
END:VEVENT
